# Void Fluid Driller tooltip
vmd.mbtt.machine_type=Void Fluid Driller
vmd.mbtt.info.1=Taps the underground fluids of a chosen dimension without drilling pipes and without depleting chunk veins.
vmd.mbtt.info.2=Put a Dimension Display block into the controller slot to select the dimension; leave the slot empty to use the dimension the machine is built in.
vmd.mbtt.info.3=A programmed circuit (configuration 1..N) in the input bus selects the N-th fluid of that dimension's fluid table; configuration 0 or no circuit picks a fluid by weighted random (weights = generation chance).
vmd.mbtt.info.4=A circuit configuration beyond the fluid count of the dimension fails the cycle with an error message.
vmd.mbtt.info.5=Drill heads in the input bus boost the output: Iron x1.25, Steel x1.5, Titanium x1.75, Naquadah x2.0, Infinity x3.0 (highest present applies). Each finished cycle consumes one drill head with a 0.1% chance.
vmd.mbtt.info.6=Produces 1000mB x voltage factor x drill bonus x parallel count per 100 tick cycle.
vmd.mbtt.info.7=The Infinity stage scales its parallel count with the input voltage: 8^(tier - UV), i.e. UHV=8, UEV=64, UIV=512, UMV=4096, UXV=32768, MAX=262144; the EU/t draw is multiplied by the parallel count.
vmd.mbtt.structure.front_bottom_center=Controller, front bottom center
vmd.mbtt.structure.center_shaft_frame=Frame Blocks (shaft below the controller)
vmd.mbtt.structure.frame=%s Frame Blocks (plus-shaped middle layers)
vmd.mbtt.structure.any_bottom_casing_min_tier=Any casing, min tier %s
vmd.mbtt.structure.any_bottom_casing=Any casing
vmd.mbtt.structure.input_bus=Input Bus (drill head and programmed circuit)
vmd.mbtt.structure.input_hatch=Input Hatch (optional)
vmd.mbtt.structure.output_bus=Output Bus (optional)
vmd.mbtt.structure.output_hatch=Output Hatch (fluid output, required)

