# Wooden Void Fluid Pump tooltip
vmd.pump.desc.1=Non-electric wooden pump that taps the Overworld underground fluids.
vmd.pump.desc.2=Produces 100mB every 200 ticks into its internal output tank; a full or incompatible tank stalls the machine, draw the fluid out with pipes from any non-main face.
vmd.pump.desc.3=Programmed circuit (configuration 1..N) in the circuit slot selects the N-th Overworld fluid; configuration 0 or no circuit = weighted random.
vmd.pump.desc.4=The internal tank never mixes fluids; switch the circuit only after it is drained.
vmd.pump.desc.5=The circuit slot (first input slot) only accepts programmed circuits.
vmd.pump.desc.selection=Current selection: %s
vmd.pump.selection.invalid=Invalid circuit configuration

# Wooden Void Miner
gt.blockmachines.VoidMinerWooden.name=Wooden Void Miner
gt.blockmachines.voidminerwooden.name=Wooden Void Miner

# Wooden Void Miner tooltip
vmd.miner.desc.1=Non-electric wooden miner that pulls ore items from the Overworld ore generation tables without breaking blocks.
vmd.miner.desc.2=Produces 1 ore item every 100 ticks into its output slot; a full slot stalls the machine, take the output out manually or with a conveyor.
vmd.miner.desc.3=Programmed circuit (configuration 1..N) in the circuit slot selects the N-th Overworld ore vein; configuration N+1 selects the poor (small) ore pool.
vmd.miner.desc.4=Configuration 0 or no circuit mixes all veins and poor ores into one weighted pool (weights = generation weights).
vmd.miner.desc.5=A circuit configuration beyond N+1 idles the machine; the circuit slot (first input slot) only accepts programmed circuits.
vmd.miner.desc.selection=Current selection: %s
vmd.miner.selection.poor=Poor ore pool
vmd.miner.selection.mixed=All ores (weighted)

